THIRD-PARTY ATTRIBUTION
=======================

African American English items: the ReDial dataset
--------------------------------------------------

The 20 African American English items in this repository (item IDs AAE00 to
AAE19 in items/items.csv, and items/sources/aae_items.json) are derived from
the ReDial dataset released with:

    Fangru Lin, Shaoguang Mao, Emanuele La Malfa, Valentin Hofmann,
    Adrian de Wynter, Xun Wang, Si-Qing Chen, Michael Wooldridge,
    Janet B. Pierrehumbert, Furu Wei.
    "Assessing Dialect Fairness and Robustness of Large Language Models in
    Reasoning Tasks." Proceedings of the 63rd Annual Meeting of the
    Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL), 2025.
    https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2410.11005

    Source repository: https://github.com/fangru-lin/redial_dialect_robustness_fairness
    Dataset card:      https://huggingface.co/datasets/fangrulin/redial

Licence
-------

ReDial is released under the MIT Licence. This was confirmed from two
independent sources on 25 July 2026: the licence indicator on the GitHub
repository page, and the "License Identifier: MIT" field on the Hugging Face
dataset card. The MIT Licence permits redistribution with attribution, which
is the basis on which these items are included here.

Disclosure: at the time of assembly the body of the ReDial LICENSE file could
not be retrieved directly (raw.githubusercontent.com returned 404 on both the
main and master branches, and the GitHub API was unavailable from the
assembling environment). The licence identifier is therefore quoted from the
two sources above rather than transcribed from their LICENSE file. If the
ReDial authors consider this attribution insufficient or incorrect, we will
correct or remove the items on request.

Stated scope of use, quoted verbatim from the ReDial dataset card
------------------------------------------------------------------

    Direct Use: "This is a reasoning dataset created by rewriting 7 existing
    benchmarks...could be used for research on testing language models'
    reasoning fairness and robustness towards AAVE users."

    Out-of-Scope Use: "This dataset is not intended for use in educational
    systems or organizations, or for use in health systems."

The present study is research on language model reasoning fairness towards
AAVE users, which falls within the stated Direct Use. It is not deployed in an
educational or health system.

What was changed
----------------

One ReDial item was excluded from this study's primary analysis: AAE08, the
gingerbread and apple pie problem (RowIdx 8 of the source set). Its
constraints are mutually contradictory and its two arms are not
meaning-identical. The full reasoning, with both wordings quoted, is in
docs/analysis.md section 1. The item is retained in items/items.csv and in
data/raw_responses.jsonl, and every headline figure is reported both with and
without it. This is a defect in one item, identified independently by two
separate analyses; it is not a criticism of the dataset as a whole.

The Standard American English counterparts of these items are reproduced from
ReDial as supplied.

Indian English items
--------------------

The 32 Indian English items (IE01 to IE32) were written by the author from
published grammatical descriptions of the variety, principally:

    P. Sailaja. "Indian English." Edinburgh University Press, 2009.

They have not been validated by native Indian English speakers. This is stated
as a limitation in the manuscript and is repeated here.
